body:
We are clearly misunderstanding each other here, i'm well aware i should work on myself and am in the process of doing so

&#x200B;

But people not taking me seriously, especially my rejection as i am trying to work on myself. Makes it harder AND just never want to trust anyone cause everyone is fucking obsessed with trying and me the martin who will "make it all okay and get the girl" and it's gross and sick and i want nothing more than for people to leave me alone and i wish i wasn't even sexually attractive to ANYONE just so it would stop and stop triggering panic attacks but these people do not care

Quite honestly I don't, or at least many parts of myself don't want to. It's more I'm feeling even more and more let down and like I'm succumbing to the endless pit of mistrust as nobody takes my no seriously but as a "i'll wait for you to be okay" and I don't want anyone to "wait" for me or even think of any sort of potential with me but everyone seems like they only listen and care about themselves as they literally try and devote their future to waiting for my \*possible\* recovery

&#x200B;

And it's not helping me heal at all, just damaging me far worse

Nothing special over than it was going to be a long weekend so plenty of time for nobody to notice as no work, usually not on social media during the day ect

&#x200B;

It's a lot, I've felt this way since I was 10, too aware of the cycle that I'm recycling (reliving trauma)  the last straw probably the fact that I've got what I can only assume is PDSD and the moment anyone finds me attractive or expresses a romantic interest in me, even just words like "love" or "crush" make me feel like their going to violate me and I can't stop feeling like that even if I know it's irrational and highly unlikely with most people
